textContent:
CSS Lists are used to display items in a clear and organized manner, either with bullets (unordered) or numbers (ordered).CSS lists help present items in an organized way using bullets or numbers, making webpage content clear and easy to read.CSS allows customization of list styles, improving the visual design and layout of list elements.Try It:
        .custom-item {
          border: 1px solid gray;
          font-family: 'Gill Sans', 'Gill Sans MT', Calibri, 'Trebuchet MS',
            sans-serif;
          border-radius: 3px;
          margin: auto;
          margin-top: 5px;
          max-width: 320px;
          min-width: 180px;
          width: 80%;
          cursor: pointer;
          background-color: rgb(133, 173, 179);
          color: rgb(255, 255, 255);
          font-weight: 600;
          letter-spacing: 1.5px;
          padding: 5px;
          font-size: 13px;
        }
        .custom-item:hover {
          box-shadow: 0 0 2px grey;
          background-color: rgb(57, 149, 163);
          color: white;
        }
        .activeItem {
          background-color: rgb(57, 149, 163);
          color: white;
        }
        @media screen and (max-width: 500px) {
          .custom-container {
            flex-direction: column;
          }
          .custom-snippets {
            border-right: none !important;
            border-bottom: 2px solid;
            width: 100% !important;
            padding-bottom: 10px;
          }
        }
        .outline-box {
          width: 180px;
          height: 100px;
          background-color: #f5f5f5;
          border: 3px solid transparent;
          display: flex;
          flex-direction: column;
          justify-content: center;
          align-items: center;
          text-align: center;
          transition: all 0.5s;
          margin: 20px;
          box-sizing: border-box;
          background-color: rgb(180, 219, 206);
        }
        .outline-box:hover {
          outline-color: #ff6f61;
        }
        .box-info {
          font-size: 12px;
          color: #777;
          margin-top: 5px;
        }
        .box-info span {
          font-weight: bold;
          color: #333;
        }

